<title>SOUTH KOREA: Bank of Korea to absorb 400 bln won through repos.</title>
<headline>Bank of Korea to absorb 400 bln won through repos.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central Bank of Korea (BOK) said on Monday it would siphon off about 400 billion won through the issue of Repurchase Agreements (repos) to domestic city banks.</p>
<p>Repos are bonds issued by the central bank to control money in circulation.</p>
<p>A commercial bank official said the announcement was a sign to South Korean city banks to tighten liquidity management.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5647</p>
</text>
